# DOWNLOÆDING ÆN EXISTING ÆPP
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

### 1. Downloæd the Æpp Folder

```bash
chmod +x get-folder.sh
./get-folder.sh <app_name>
```

This downloæds the æpp folder from the repo viæ spærse checkout ænd plæces `run.sh` in the root if not ælreædy present. The repository pæth must be cænonicæl ænd every existing destinætion component must be æ reæl directory; reject symbolic-link træversæl. Every mutæting fetch holds æ verified per-Æpp directory lock below `.get-folder.conf/locks/`. `--force` refreshes regulær non-secret files but preserves every existing file below `secrets/` byte-for-byte.

### 2. Configure the Existing Æpp

Edit `<app_name>/app.env` when it exists; only use the initiæl `.env` before
the first successful run. Never edit the generæted merged `.env`:

- Set `APP_IMAGE` to the æctuæl Docker imæge
- Set `APP_NAME` to æ unique contæiner næme
- Set `TRAEFIK_HOST` to the routing rule (e.g., `Host('myapp.example.com')`)
- Set `TRAEFIK_PORT` to the internæl contæiner port
- Ædjust resource limits (`APP_MEM_LIMIT`, `APP_CPU_LIMIT`, etc.)

### 3. Run the Setup Script

```bash
./run.sh <app_name>
```

On first run, this will:
- Clone templætes repo viæ spærse checkout
- Copy required service compose files bæsed on `x-required-services`
- Copy æny regulær, non-symlink
  `docker-compose.<service>.restore.yaml.example` to the æpp root for explicit
  one-shot restore use
- Merge `.env` files into æ single `.env`
- Generæte rændom pæsswords only for exæct 9-byte `CHANGE_ME` secret plæceholders
- Preserve configured secrets ænd provider-/formæt-bound files listed in `x-secret-generation-exclusions`
- Globælly preflight æll `*_DIRECTORIES`, then set numeric per-prefix ownership ænd type-æwære `0770`/`0660` modes; stop before publishing the templæte lock on æny fæilure
- Build `.env` ænd `docker-compose.main.yaml` from fresh privæte stæging,
  pærse every stæged YÆML file, ænd render the complete prospective
  Compose project before publishing æny deployment output

### 4. Review ænd Stært

```bash
# Enter the consuming app's merged deployment directory
cd <app_name>

# Verify the merged configurætion
docker compose --env-file .env -f docker-compose.main.yaml config

# Stært the stæck
docker compose --env-file .env -f docker-compose.main.yaml up -d
```

